mm8108-driver (2.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * debian/mm8108-driver-dkms.dkms: pass KERNEL_SRC. Upstream's Makefile
    adds '-I$(KERNEL_SRC)' right before '-DCONFIG_MORSE_SDIO'; with
    KERNEL_SRC unset the bare '-I' consumed that define, so the SDIO bus
    driver was never registered.
  * debian/mm8108-driver-dkms.dkms: build with CONFIG_MORSE_SDIO_ALIGNMENT=4
    so bulk SDIO buffers meet the 4-byte DMA alignment required by common
    SBC MMC hosts (sunxi-mmc, dw_mmc, meson-gx-mmc); upstream defaults to 2.
  * debian/mm8108-driver-dkms.dkms: build with CONFIG_MORSE_COUNTRY=US to
    default the 'country' module parameter to US instead of upstream's AU.
  * debian/mm8108-driver-dkms.dkms: build with CONFIG_MORSE_POWERSAVE_MODE=0
    to disable power save by default (the 'enable_ps' module parameter);
    upstream defaults to fully enabled.

 -- Austin <vidplace7@gmail.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

mm8108-driver (2.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release (upstream tag mm8108-2.1.0).
  * debian/watch: track the per-chip 'mm8108-' tags; upstream now tags the
    MM6108 and MM8108 series separately.
  * debian/watch: match the archive extension in filenamemangle so the
    downloaded tarball is not named mm8108-driver-<version>.tar.gz.tar.gz.
  * debian/rules: clone the 'mm8108-<upstream version>' tag in
    get-orig-source, derived from the changelog version.
  * debian/copyright: declare the upstream license as GPL-2.0-or-later to
    match the SPDX headers in the upstream sources, and extend the copyright
    years to 2026.

 -- Austin <vidplace7@gmail.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

mm8108-driver (1.17.9-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Split morse-driver into per-chip packages; this is the MM8108 variant.
  * Rename source package to mm8108-driver and binary package to
    mm8108-driver-dkms.
  * Rename the DKMS module tree to /usr/src/mm8108-driver-<version>.
  * Recommend mm8108-firmware instead of morse-firmware.
  * Conflict with mm6108-driver-dkms; the two chip variants are mutually
    exclusive.

